# Reason: Ren'Py 7 games made before 7.8.3. Ren'Py 7.8.3 and 8.3.3 added "End an obsolete ongoing transition" in `Interface.interact_core` (upstream 937c91f, renpy issue #5827: a custom Quick Menu button blocked other input after a transition). It restarts the interaction when the ongoing transition of the top layer has expired, and the restart makes `screen.per_interact` evaluate every shown screen a second time. Earlier engines do not restart there. LuckyParadox (7.4.11) rolls `renpy.random.choice` in its main menu screen, so 0.5 s after the menu appears (end of `config.enter_transition`) the background re-rolled and cut to another image. The pops stay; the restart is skipped when `renpy.lexer.renpy7_syntax` is set (Ren'Py 7 detection) and the game's `config.script_version` is unknown or older than 7.8.3. Games made with 7.8.3 or later keep the restart, as on their own engine.

diff --git a/renpy/display/core.py b/renpy/display/core.py
--- a/renpy/display/core.py
+++ b/renpy/display/core.py
@@ -2921,8 +2921,13 @@
                     self.ongoing_transition.pop(None, None)
                     self.transition_time.pop(None, None)
                     self.transition_from.pop(None, None)
-                    self.restart_interaction = True
 
+                    # Player patch: Ren'Py 7 before 7.8.3 never restarted here, and a restart
+                    # evaluates the screens again (a `renpy.random.choice` in a screen then re-rolls).
+                    sv = renpy.config.script_version
+                    if not (renpy.lexer.renpy7_syntax and (sv is None or tuple(sv) < (7, 8, 3))):
+                        self.restart_interaction = True
+
                 # See if we want to restart the interaction entirely.
                 if self.restart_interaction and not self.display_reset:
                     return True, None
